### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### PROGRAM SERVICE (via Gateway :8080)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Create Program - Computer Science
POST http://localhost:8080/programs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Computer Science",
  "description": "Bachelor degree in Computer Science",
  "durationYears": 3
}

###

### 2. Create Program - Mathematics
POST http://localhost:8080/programs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mathematics",
  "description": "Bachelor degree in Mathematics",
  "durationYears": 3
}

###

### 3. Get All Programs
GET http://localhost:8080/programs

###

### 4. Get Program by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/programs/1

###

### 5. Update Program
PUT http://localhost:8080/programs/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Computer Science",
  "description": "Updated: Bachelor degree in CS and Software Engineering",
  "durationYears": 4
}

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STUDENT SERVICE (via Gateway :8080)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────

### 6. Create Student (linked to Program 1)
POST http://localhost:8080/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Zakaria",
  "lastName": "Aissari",
  "email": "zakaria@example.com",
  "programId": 1
}

###

### 7. Create Second Student
POST http://localhost:8080/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Amine",
  "lastName": "Benali",
  "email": "amine@example.com",
  "programId": 2
}

###

### 8. Get All Students (each includes program details)
GET http://localhost:8080/students

###

### 9. Get Student by ID (shows embedded program object)
GET http://localhost:8080/students/1

###

### 10. Update Student
PUT http://localhost:8080/students/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Zakaria",
  "lastName": "Aissari",
  "email": "zakaria.updated@example.com",
  "programId": 1
}

###

### 11. Delete Student
DELETE http://localhost:8080/students/2

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### ERROR CASES - Test your error handling
### ─────────────────────────────────────────

### 12. Get non-existent student → expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/students/999

###

### 13. Create student with invalid data → expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "programId": null
}

###

### 14. Create duplicate email → expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "zakaria.updated@example.com",
  "programId": 1
}

###

### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### NOTE SERVICE (via Gateway :8080)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────

### 15. Create Note for Student 1 - Mathematics
POST http://localhost:8080/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 1,
  "subject": "Mathematics",
  "value": 16.5,
  "comment": "Excellent work"
}

###

### 16. Create Note for Student 1 - Physics
POST http://localhost:8080/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 1,
  "subject": "Physics",
  "value": 14.0,
  "comment": "Good progress"
}

###

### 17. Create Note for Student 2 - Algorithms
POST http://localhost:8080/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 2,
  "subject": "Algorithms",
  "value": 18.0,
  "comment": "Outstanding"
}

###

### 18. Get All Notes
GET http://localhost:8080/notes

###

### 19. Get Note by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/notes/1

###

### 20. Get All Notes for Student 1
GET http://localhost:8080/notes/student/1

###

### 21. Update Note
PUT http://localhost:8080/notes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 1,
  "subject": "Mathematics",
  "value": 17.5,
  "comment": "Revised after correction"
}

###

### 22. Delete Note
DELETE http://localhost:8080/notes/3

###

### 23. Get non-existent note → expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/notes/999

###

### 24. Create note with invalid value → expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 1,
  "subject": "Math",
  "value": 25,
  "comment": "Invalid grade"
}

###

